      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $-\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The number $-\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ is a negative irrational number. It is not a rational number.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{C}$ contains all complex numbers. Therefore, $-\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{C}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. Therefore, $-\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$ contains the positive real numbers. Therefore, $-\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{R}^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. Therefore, $-\\frac{1}{\\pi}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{C}$, $\\mathbb{R}$, $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ only.",
