      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the negative rational numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the negative rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative integers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative rational numbers. For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative rational numbers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{N}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative rational numbers.\n\nTherefore, select none of the sets; leave every box unchecked.",
